        {
          "unit_id": "around_town",
          "title": "Where's the Supermarket?",
          "description": "Pregunta y da direcciones con preposiciones de lugar e imperativos. Y para comparar sitios: bigger than, the biggest.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "around_town_lesson",
              "title": "Prepositions of place and directions",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Where's the supermarket?",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Lucía! Hi! What's the craic?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Sorry? The… craic?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Ha, sorry. It's Irish. It means \"How are you?\""
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Oh! I'm fine. But I'm lost. Is there a supermarket near here?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Yes, there's one on Park Street. Go straight on, then turn left at the bank."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Straight on, then left at the bank…"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "That's it. The supermarket is next to a café, opposite the cinema."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Is there a chemist's near here too?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Yes. It's between the post office and the bookshop."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Thanks, Daniel. You're very kind."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Ah, sure it's no bother. Come with me. I want a coffee from that café!"
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "Saturday morning. Lucía needs some food, but where is the supermarket? She walks near the harbour and she sees a friendly face."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"It's between the post office and the bookshop.\" Between = …",
                        "options": [
                          "entre",
                          "enfrente de",
                          "al lado de"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"opposite the cinema\" = …",
                        "options": [
                          "enfrente del cine",
                          "detrás del cine",
                          "dentro del cine"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"Turn left at the bank.\" This is…",
                        "options": [
                          "an instruction",
                          "a question",
                          "a past action"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0,
                        "explanation": "Es un imperativo: el verbo sin sujeto."
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"What's the craic?\" means…",
                        "options": [
                          "How are you?",
                          "What time is it?",
                          "Where are you?"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0,
                        "explanation": "Expresión irlandesa muy coloquial."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Prepositions of place and the imperative",
                    "explanation": "Las preposiciones de lugar dicen dónde está algo: The supermarket is next to a café. Con calles se usa on: on Park Street.\n\nPara dar indicaciones usamos el imperativo, es decir, el verbo sin sujeto: Go straight on. Turn left. Take the second right. En negativo, con don't: Don't turn right.\n\nPara preguntar: Is there a … near here? o Excuse me, where's the …?\n\nOjo con un falso amigo: bookshop = librería; library = biblioteca.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Preposición",
                        "Significado",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "next to",
                          "al lado de",
                          "The supermarket is next to a café."
                        ],
                        [
                          "opposite",
                          "enfrente de",
                          "It's opposite the cinema."
                        ],
                        [
                          "between",
                          "entre",
                          "The chemist's is between the post office and the bookshop."
                        ],
                        [
                          "behind",
                          "detrás de",
                          "The garden is behind the house."
                        ],
                        [
                          "in front of",
                          "delante de",
                          "The bus stop is in front of the bank."
                        ],
                        [
                          "near",
                          "cerca de",
                          "There's a supermarket near here."
                        ],
                        [
                          "on",
                          "en (una calle)",
                          "It's on Park Street."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Go straight on, then turn left at the bank.",
                      "The supermarket is next to a café, opposite the cinema.",
                      "Is there a chemist's near here?",
                      "Don't turn right!"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Comparing places: bigger than, the biggest",
                    "explanation": "Para comparar dos cosas usamos el adjetivo + -er + than: The supermarket is bigger than the corner shop. Con adjetivos largos se pone more delante: The park is more beautiful than the square.\n\nPara decir que algo es «el más…» de un grupo usamos the + adjetivo + -est: It's the biggest supermarket in Bristol. Con adjetivos largos: the most beautiful.\n\nCambios de ortografía: big → bigger (se dobla la consonante), nice → nicer, easy → easier.\n\nIrregulares: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → further → the furthest.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Adjetivo",
                        "Comparativo",
                        "Superlativo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "cheap",
                          "cheaper than",
                          "the cheapest"
                        ],
                        [
                          "big",
                          "bigger than",
                          "the biggest"
                        ],
                        [
                          "beautiful",
                          "more beautiful than",
                          "the most beautiful"
                        ],
                        [
                          "good",
                          "better than",
                          "the best"
                        ],
                        [
                          "far",
                          "further than",
                          "the furthest"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "The supermarket is bigger than the corner shop.",
                      "The bus is cheaper than a taxi.",
                      "It's the best café in Clifton.",
                      "The station is further than the park."
                    ]
                  }
                },
